WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.480
Mind Your Decisions! I'm Presh Talwalkar

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:09.040
The product of three integers x, y and z is 192.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.720
z = 4 and p is equal to the average of x and y.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.640
What is the minimum possible value of p?

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.600
The answer choices are 6, 7, 8 and 9.5.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.360
This was asked on the 2019 GATE exam conducted by IIT in India.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.360
Thanks to Manjeet for the suggestion!

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.360
Pause the video if you'd like to give this problem a try,

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.880
and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve the problem.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.480
We'll solve this problem step by step.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:58.120
First x times y times z is equal to 192.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.160
Then z is equal to 4.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.000
We substitute and then divide both sides by 4.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.080
This means x times y is equal to 48.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.640
p is equal to the average of x and y.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.040
Thus, p is equal to x plus y, all over two.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.200
We want the minimum value of p.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:23.400
This will be the minimum value of x plus y, all over two.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.660
How do we proceed from here?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.480
Recall that x and y are integers.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:32.760
We have x times y is equal to 48.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.080
So we'll consider the integer factors of 48.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.840
So we'll write out the possibilities for the factors of 48.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.640
We then calculate the average values.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.880
It would appear the lowest average value is seven.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.920
But this is not the correct answer!

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.520
The reason is that x and y are integers.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.960
Therefore x and y can also take negative values.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.400
Notice if we multiply both x and y by negative one,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.240
we also get valid possibilities,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.560
and the lowest possibile value for their average will be -24.5.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.840
And that's the correct answer to this question!

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:19.280
The testing agency admitted the mistake and gave full marks to everyone!

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:25.720
There is a lesson: the correct answer was not included as one of the answer choices on the test!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:29.860
You should always be careful in the assumptions you make in mathematics!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:34.420
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube!

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.700
As always: Thanks for watching and Thanks for your support!

00:02:38.820 --> 02:46:38.080
*awesome outro song plays*

